-- title:
--   Second inequality for Galois cubic extensions
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $E$ be number fields (fields of characteristic $0$, finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, living in universes $u$ and $v$ respectively) with $E$ a $k$-algebra, let $\mathrm{finrank}_k E = 3$, assume $E/k$ is Galois, and let $\mathfrak{f}$ be an ideal of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_k$. The conclusion is the predicate [`LanglandsTunnell.P2.Artin.SecondInequalityCTM k E 𝔣`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ArtinCoreCTM.html#L331), which asserts the following divisibility: inside the group `coprimeToModulus k 𝔣` of objects attached to $k$ coprime to the modulus $\mathfrak{f}$, form the subgroup `normRaySubgroup k E 𝔣` given by the join (the subgroup generated by the union) of two subgroups, namely the narrow ray subgroup `narrowRaySubgroup k 𝔣` modulo $\mathfrak{f}$, viewed as a subgroup of `coprimeToModulus k 𝔣`, and the range of the relative norm homomorphism [`HeckeCharacter.relNormCTM k E 𝔣`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ArtinCoreCTM.html#L69) coming from the extension $E/k$; then the index of this subgroup divides `Nat.card (E ≃ₐ[k] E)`, the cardinality of the group of $k$-algebra automorphisms of $E$, which under the stated hypotheses is $3$. No hypothesis that $k$ contains a primitive cube root of unity is imposed, and no hypothesis is placed on $\mathfrak{f}$.
--
--   This is the second inequality of class field theory for a cyclic cubic layer, in the form bounding the index of the product of the narrow ray group and the group of relative norms by the degree of the extension, stated for an arbitrary base number field. It is used in the construction of transfer data for degree-three Galois extensions, via [`LanglandsTunnell.Artin.exists_transferData_of_finrank_eq_three`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.Artin.exists_transferData_of_finrank_eq_three), within the Langlands–Tunnell input to the argument.
